      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan, we need to convert the cost from Namibian dollars to US dollars, and then from US dollars to Chinese yuan. Here are the steps to solve the problem:\n\n1. **Convert Namibian dollars to US dollars:**\n   The problem states that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. Therefore, the cost of the painting in US dollars is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105 \\text{ Namibian dollars}}{7 \\text{ Namibian dollars/US dollar}} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert US dollars to Chinese yuan:**\n   The problem states that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. Therefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan/US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
