    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars (NAD) to Chinese yuan (CNY). We know the following exchange rates:\n\n1 USD = 7 NAD\n1 USD = 6 CNY\n\nFirst, we need to find out how many US dollars it takes to get 105 NAD. We can do this by dividing 105 NAD by the exchange rate of 7 NAD per USD:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Number of USD} = \\frac{105 \\text{ NAD}}{7 \\text{ NAD/USD}} = 15 \\text{ USD}\n\\]\n\nNow that we know the painting costs 15 USD, we can convert this amount to CNY using the exchange rate of 6 CNY per USD:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in CNY} = 15 \\text{ USD} \\times 6 \\text{ CNY/USD} = 90 \\text{ CNY}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\boxed{90}.",
